    "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!}\\), we will first simplify the expression step by step.\n\n1. **Rewrite the factorial expressions:**\n   \\[\n   (N-1)! = (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (N+1)! = (N+1) \\times N \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Express the numerator:**\n   \\[\n   (N-1)!(N) = (N-1) \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1 \\times N\n   \\]\n\n3. **Express the denominator:**\n   \\[\n   (N+1)! = (N+1) \\times N \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine the numerator and the denominator:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!} = \\frac{(N-1) \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1 \\times N}{(N+1) \\times N \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Cancel out the common terms:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(N-1) \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1 \\times N}{(N+1) \\times N \\times (N-1) \\times (N-2) \\times \\cdots \\times 1} = \\frac{N}{N+1}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the fraction:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{N}{N+1} = \\frac{N}{N+1}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{N}{N+1}}\n\\]",
